 "text": "Lleu Llaw Gyffes is a Welsh god or hero whose name means the bright one of the skilful hand. He is a son of the goddess ARIANRHOD and a ward of the sorcerer GWYDION. Gwydion drew his sister into granting the lad his name and then his arms. In the MABINOGION, Lleu later won to wife a maiden made of flowers named BLODEUWEDD. She turned to another and sought to end him. Lleu could not be slain within a hall nor without, nor on horseback nor afoot. Blodeuwedd goaded him to stand beneath a thatched roof with one foot on a deer, and at that spot he was struck and fled in the shape of an EAGLE. The tale may pair him with the Irish LUGH, yet the two carry little in common.",
 "okr": {
